---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Company"
  description="ACQI Technologies is in formation. What we are building, how we intend to operate, and what we will not do."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1 reveal">Company</p>
      <h1 class="reveal reveal-2">A company in formation, saying so on its own website.</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal reveal-3">
        ACQI Technologies is not yet an incorporated entity. That fact appears in the footer of
        every page until it stops being true. This page explains what exists, what does not, and
        what we are building toward.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">I</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">What we are building</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--sidebar">
        <div>
          <p class="lede mb-0">
            Software that reads an acquisition target's technology estate and keeps that reading
            usable from the first diligence request to the last post-close ticket.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Integration work is usually done twice. Once in diligence, by people building a
            spreadsheet under time pressure. Again after close, by people who cannot see the
            spreadsheet and do not trust it. The cost is not the duplicated effort. It is the
            decisions taken on the second reading that contradict the first.
          </p>
          <p>
            We think the fix is structural: one evidence set, with provenance, that every later
            stage reads from. That is the whole product thesis. Everything in
            <a href="/platform/">the platform</a> follows from it.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0">
            We also think it has to run inside the customer's boundary. A target's estate is not
            something to route through a vendor's tenancy during a live transaction. That
            constraint shapes the architecture, the commercial model and the way we support
            customers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">II</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">How we intend to operate</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cols cols--3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Say the uncomfortable thing early</h3>
          <p>If a gap in the product loses us a deal, that is cheaper than a customer discovering the gap in week six. The status page exists for this reason.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>No borrowed credibility</h3>
          <p>No customer logos before there are customers who have agreed to be named. No certification badges before the certificate exists. No invented adoption figures.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Confidentiality is the product</h3>
          <p>We handle estate data for a living. A customer's sector, deal and findings are not marketing material, and permission to mention them is asked in writing or not at all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Small surface, deep function</h3>
          <p>We would rather cover five stages properly than fifteen badly. The product should not have a surface that exists only to fill a menu.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Reversible by default</h3>
          <p>Merges can be undone. Migration actions are approved, not automatic. Exports are documented. A customer should always be able to leave.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Write it down</h3>
          <p>Decisions, assumptions and conflicts are recorded with an owner. Undocumented decisions are the reason the second reading of an estate disagrees with the first.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section__head">
        <span class="section__num">III</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">Current position</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="defs">
        <div>
          <dt>Legal status</dt>
          <dd>In formation. No company number, registered office or VAT registration exists yet. Contracts are made with the founders personally until incorporation.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Product stage</dt>
          <dd>Active development with design partners. Paid production deployments begin after the entity exists and the first security review is complete.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Funding</dt>
          <dd>Founder-funded. No round has closed and no investor is announced. If that changes, it will be stated here with the date.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Team</dt>
          <dd>Founder-led, with a small number of contract engineers. We do not publish headcount as a credibility signal.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Certifications</dt>
          <dd>None held. See <a href="/security/">security</a> for what is planned and when.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Trading name</dt>
          <dd>ACQI Technologies. The wordmark and the name are used by the founders ahead of incorporation.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="cols cols--2">
          <div>
            <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">Contact</p>
            <h2 class="mb-1">One address reaches a person.</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
              There is no support portal and no ticket queue yet. Mail goes to a founder and is
              answered by one.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="mb-1"><a href={`mailto:${SITE.generalEmail}`}>{SITE.generalEmail}</a> for everything commercial.</p>
            <p class="mb-1"><a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a> for vulnerabilities and security questions.</p>
            <p class="mb-0"><a href="/contact/">Contact form</a>, if you would rather not use mail.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
